#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501271} :activity/id #uuid "1bb1f997-9fe0-5e94-89c4-95bbb97a3f25" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048947 :topic/id #uuid "ce6678f7-de9f-5b74-8e66-34eb49059878" :topic/math-academy-id 2089} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501249 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "723e3a62-46ce-5ee6-be5e-b0279857a9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500703} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d2b8dd-5f5f-52c7-96a0-69db153bcf1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500811} {:answer/id #uuid "b955f10c-6517-5613-89c0-cd74c1bd80e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500853} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ef1d32-7b15-5903-9f86-c77ba3d1ed42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500868} {:answer/id #uuid "c463bc91-5bc4-5fe6-8a76-c801e96b0282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500881}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500868} :answer-field/id #uuid "899ae17d-d211-5d95-aea6-b05439a6e74e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b525e6cc-0aa9-5691-bec6-c50f5a129f63" :question/math-academy-id "q-110493" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "12f00de3-338f-56d2-8859-359b23733d90"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501251 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13bc40a4-7ba5-59a5-b74f-2c70c1d57fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500509} {:answer/id #uuid "30e849f9-e43f-555b-a478-500db4d039c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500568} {:answer/id #uuid "7b5cda25-da79-5687-8995-ce9b1f970246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500721} {:answer/id #uuid "e82c35de-863c-511b-a81e-9e222e86b84a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500961} {:answer/id #uuid "f62fa805-14d4-5eca-a0fc-bac68f968347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500993}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500993} :answer-field/id #uuid "77e9d5df-e744-5f1a-a0b6-526894e2a1eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f10c9aaf-98e6-52a7-9de1-c8d29489c892" :question/math-academy-id "q-75161" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "178fbde8-4f97-53f7-bac7-f88af87a8d55" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501273}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501260 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2098f34e-7ee7-5d3d-bd3c-1f8735d768a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500534} {:answer/id #uuid "7ccc0a60-4b27-5edb-8671-320f41c1b168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500726} {:answer/id #uuid "a50d1571-c3e3-55f4-b6ed-ba6a11704549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500803} {:answer/id #uuid "daefc58c-d127-56af-8c6e-929a2dd275ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500933} {:answer/id #uuid "e220b937-6a5e-59d2-a5d5-41a83c7a2d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500945}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500534} :answer-field/id #uuid "a301872e-f9c1-5a36-8e8e-3c31baa4c791" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "294d3a87-ec82-5ba0-946d-47e92c2e2260" :question/math-academy-id "q-110484" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "35bfeba7-bc18-5102-bfef-b4f07abd1425" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501249}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501271 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501159 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dbdb01d-4a57-549a-9067-c8cb88b27de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500625} {:answer/id #uuid "79c5607a-43a0-5745-b537-6b5b527d056b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500720} {:answer/id #uuid "9afac160-9dbe-590b-ab9a-9db17e13cb3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500781} {:answer/id #uuid "ae9e4fdb-1a23-5b1f-8e61-e96e8df1fb9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500831} {:answer/id #uuid "d11dd33f-db9a-51ba-8754-048bb7b19980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500916}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500916} :answer-field/id #uuid "07dcfd9e-686a-5980-8030-4e14ec2230eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3bf6c999-4f9a-599b-886e-437d5517ddbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-75111" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6480aa5b-ee2d-59de-9bc0-5718af92cb12" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501251}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501273 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63b5ca94-7c8e-5598-ba13-28752852bfd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500675} {:answer/id #uuid "73e152b8-77cd-51bf-ac4c-ac4a654611e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500704} {:answer/id #uuid "aa17b4c3-3333-5dcb-aee8-13cca8125a67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500818} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a14f61-2fc3-556c-8f5f-f4e80923c57d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500847} {:answer/id #uuid "bc57dbd1-cb18-5136-86e5-420e461ef7af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500859}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500675} :answer-field/id #uuid "a16204f8-f3d9-5011-8c48-c6b5f2db3a5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "62e49a58-91d5-5a4c-a1e9-c098f0c19c7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110472" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "727f72d3-00f6-53d2-92f4-c727184c4dcb" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501260}}] :activity/title "Row Operations on 3x3 Matrices as Products of Elementary Matrices" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500460}]}
